                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-25",
                                    "linecount": 47,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 577.0, 927.0 ],
                                    "text": "================================================================================\nlp_cat_dual_svf_ladder — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nWHAT IT IS\nOctave CAT style 24 dB/oct lowpass: two 2-pole state-variable sections in\nseries inside one feedback loop, instead of the Moog's four 1-pole stages.\nRounder and vocal at low damping, closer to a Moog at high damping. The loop\ninput is saturated, so self-oscillation stays bounded.\n\nSource: Werner & McClellan, DAFx-20 paper 70 §2–3.1 (Eq. 2–10, \"~CAT\" with\nequal section damping); McClellan, DAFx-26 paper 28 (stability of the\ntrapezoidal SVF and ladder under modulation).\n\nPARAMETERS (4)\n\n1. damping — 0.2…1.2, default 0.7\n   Damping r of each SVF section. 1.064 is the original CAT; lower values\n   make each section peaky, so the filter gets a vowel-like hump even with\n   no resonance.\n\n2. drive_db — 0…24 dB, default 6 dB\n   Saturation at the loop input. Small-signal gain stays at unity; more\n   drive = grittier resonance and a quieter self-oscillation.\n\n3. freq_offset_st — -36…+36 semitones, default 0\n   Transposes the cutoff that arrives on in3.\n\n4. width — 0…100 %, default 50 %\n   Adds a side signal from a copy of the filter tuned up to +1 octave (at\n   100 %). L hears the brighter copy, R its mirror image; L+R is exactly the\n   plain filter, so mono is unaffected.\n\nINLETS / OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: stereo audio.  out1 / out2: stereo.\n- in3: cutoff in Hz. Values <= 1 Hz are ignored (last value held, 600 Hz at\n  start).\n- in4: resonance 0…1 (1 = edge of self-oscillation). 0 or unpatched = no\n  resonance, still a 24 dB lowpass.\n\nNOTES\n- Gain staging: feedback cuts the passband by up to 15 dB; half of that is\n  made up (sqrt(1 + 4 r^2 k)), and half the extra section peak is removed\n  when damping < 0.707, so turning resonance up thins the sound instead of\n  making it louder.\n- in3 / in4 are smoothed over 5 ms.\n- No safety limiter.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
